  "tagline": "An SQS-style message queue implemented as a lightweight Postgres extension.",
  "description": "PGMQ gives Postgres an SQS-like queue API: send, read with a visibility timeout, archive and delete, all as SQL functions over ordinary tables. Because messages live in Postgres, enqueueing can join the same transaction as your business writes, removing dual-write problems, and you avoid running a separate broker. Originally built at Tembo, the project now lives in its own community GitHub organization, is written in plain SQL so it installs even on managed Postgres without custom binaries, and is bundled by Supabase as Supabase Queues. Expect thousands, not millions, of messages per second.",
